[?2004lopinav[?2004h>         "answer": "Paxlovid is contraindicated with drugs that are primarily metabolized by CYP3A and for which elevated concentrations are associated with serious and/or life-threatening reactions. These include: alfuzosin; ranolazine; amiodarone, dronedarone, flecainide, propafenone, quinidine; colchicine (in patients with renal and/or hepatic impairment); lurasidone, pimozide; silodosin; eplerenone, ivabradine; dihydroergotamine, ergotamine, methylergonovine; lovastatin, simvastatin; voclosporin; lomitapide; eletriptan, ubrogepant; finerenone; naloxegol; sildenafil (Revatio) when used for PAH; triazolam, oral midazolam; flibanserin; and tolvaptan. Additionally, it is contraindicated with strong CYP3A inducers where significantly reduced nirmatrelvir or ritonavir plasma concentrations can cause loss of virologic response and resistance, including: apalutamide, enzalutamide; carbamazepine, phenobarbital, primidone, phenytoin; rifampin, rifapentine; lumacaftor/ivacaftor; and St. John's Wort.",
