           [?2004h>         "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "Lopinavir-Ritonavir can be given in once daily or twice daily dosing regimens in adults. The recommended once daily regimen is 800 mg/200 mg (10 mL of 80 mg/20 mg per mL oral solution) once daily. The recommended twice daily regimen is 400 mg/100 mg (5 mL) twice daily. The once daily regimen is not recommended in pediatric patients, pregnant women, in combination with strong CYP3A inducers (carbamazepine, phenobarbital, phenytoin) or certain antiretrovirals (efavirenz, nevirapine, nelfinavir), or in patients with three or more lopinavir resistance-associated substitutions. When administered in combination with efavirenz, nevirapine, or nelfinavir, the twice daily dose of Lopinavir-Ritonavir should be increased to 520 mg/130 mg (6.5 mL) twice daily.",
