[?2004l "supportin[?2004h>         "answer": "The safety risks listed for Lopinavir-Ritonavir include: (1) Toxicity in preterm neonates due to the excipients ethanol (approx. 42% v/v) and propylene glycol (approx. 15% w/v), which can accumulate and cause life-threatening cardiac toxicity, lactic acidosis, acute renal failure, CNS depression, and respiratory complications. (2) Pancreatitis, which has been observed in patients receiving therapy, sometimes leading to fatalities, particularly in patients with marked triglyceride elevations. (3) Hepatotoxicity, with reports of transaminase elevations, hepatitis, and hepatic decompensation, especially in patients with chronic hepatitis B or C or cirrhosis. (4) QT and PR interval prolongation, which can lead to cardiac conduction abnormalities, including second or third degree AV block. (5) New onset or worsening of diabetes mellitus/hyperglycemia. (6) Immune reconstitution syndrome. (7) Large lipid elevations (cholesterol and triglycerides). (8) Fat redistribution/accumulation. (9) Increased bleeding in patients with hemophilia.",
