[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "The important warnings and precautions associated with Lopinavir-Ritonavir include: (1) Serious adverse reactions due to drug interactions, as lopinavir and ritonavir is a CYP3A inhibitor. (2) Toxicity in preterm neonates due to ethanol and propylene glycol excipients in the oral solution. (3) Pancreatitis (including fatalities), requiring evaluation and potential therapy suspension if symptoms or lab abnormalities occur. (4) Hepatotoxicity, requiring close monitoring of transaminases, especially in patients with underlying hepatitis B/C or cirrhosis. (5) QT interval prolongation and torsade de pointes, necessitating avoidance in patients with congenital long QT syndrome or hypokalemia. (6) PR interval prolongation, which can cause second or third degree AV block. (7) New onset or worsening of diabetes mellitus and hyperglycemia. (8) Immune reconstitution syndrome. (9) Large lipid elevations. (10) Fat redistribution. (11) Increased bleeding in patients with hemophilia.",
